From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:03:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 07/43] Shaders: signature rows keep the console's order and
 one interpolation mode

Measured with `victory translate --validate` over all 26,148 programs of
the title, against 310c6eb: vertex and pixel programs validated
14,065 -> 14,173, mesh 8,657 -> 8,691, compute unchanged (2,722).

- Signature parts keep the console's element order instead of sorting
  by register and column: the validator rebuilds the parts from the
  metadata in element order and compares bytes, so a program listing
  TEXCOORD16 before TANGENT0 in one row was refused.
- Elements sharing a row get one interpolation mode (the validator
  refuses a row whose modes differ): the mode of the elements the
  program reads; constant when none is read, or on an output row with
  a constant member.
- A test for a 16-bit write over an f16 first half
  (PS_DeferredTextured_c5fd36bb), which the first-half fix on main
  already passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit fcabbf9e284a0698aaeb307ec8dc2ac24c49f07e)
